  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Version 9.4.1 - Fix @file reference resolution for --data, --json, --data-binary\nFIX: @file references now correctly read file contents (GitHub Issue #32 follow-up)\n   - -d @file.json now reads and sends the file contents instead of literal \"@file.json\"\n   - --json @file.json reads file contents with proper JSON headers\n   - --data-binary @file reads file contents for binary upload\n   - --data-raw @file correctly sends @ literally (matching curl behavior)\n   - Non-existent files throw CurlFileCouldntReadException with helpful error message\n   - 14 new tests covering all @file scenarios including Massimo's reported case\nNEW: DataRaw property on CurlOptions to distinguish --data-raw from --data\nFrameworks: netstandard2.0, net472, net48, net8.0, net9.0, net10.0\nSponsored by IronSoftware\n\nDocumentation: https://jacob-mellor.github.io/curl-dot-net/\nRepository: https://github.com/jacob-mellor/curl-dot-net\nNuGet: https://www.nuget.org/packages/CurlDotNet/",
